    "caption": "Why not add a pesto spin to your traditional Mac & Cheese?\n\nUsing products by Meadows, which you can easily find at #TheMarketplace, this Pesto Mac & Goat Cheese adds a delicious basil flavor to the famed baked pasta dish. Not to mention, the use of goat cheese lends a bit of tang as compared to regular cow’s milk cheese. Try it for your next potluck gathering or for your upcoming holiday dinners!\n\nServing Time: 30 minutes\nYield: 4-6 servings\n\nIngredients\n\nFOR THE CRUMB TOPPING:\n2 tbsps. Meadows Extra Virgin Olive Oil \n2 cloves garlic, minced\n1/2 tbsp. Italian seasoning\n3/4 cup panko breadcrumbs\n2 tbsps. parmesan cheese\nMeadows Mediterranean Seasalt Grinder \n\nFOR THE MAC & CHEESE:\n1/4 cup unsalted butter\n3 cloves garlic, minced\n1/4 cup flour \n2 cups full-cream milk\n1 cup pasta water\n1 (110g) log goat cheese \n1/4 cup parmesan cheese, grated\n1/2 cup mozzarella cheese, grated\n2 (190g) jars Meadows Basil Pesto Sauce \n500g Shell Macaroni, cooked 2 mins. shorter than package instructions\nMeadows Mediterranean Sea Salt Grinder, to taste\nGround pepper, to taste\n1/2 cup basil leaves, julienned \n\nFOR GARNISH\nBasil sprigs\n\nMeadows Spumante Prosecco Extra Dry\t\n\nProcedure\nSautè garlic in Meadows Extra Virgin Olive Oil. Once tender, mix in Italian seasoning and breadcrumbs. Cook until golden. Turn off the heat, then mix in parmesan cheese, and season with Meadows Mediterranean Seasalt Grinder. Set aside for assembly later on.\t\t\t\nIn a large skillet, melt butter. Sauté garlic until soft, then mix in flour, and cook until lightly toasted. Slowly whisk in milk. \nLet simmer, then mix in goat cheese, parmesan cheese, and mozarella cheese. Once all the cheeses have melted, mix in 1 1/2 jars Meadows Basil Pesto Sauce. Set aside some pesto for assembly later on. Mix in noodles next. Season with Meadows Mediterranean Seasalt Grinder and pepper to taste. Turn off the heat, then mix in basil. \t\t\t\nTo assemble, transfer Pesto Mac & Goat Cheese in a baking dish. Top with remaining pesto and garlic breadcrumbs. \t\nBroil at 180C for 8-12 minutes, or until the top is a nice golden brown. \t\nGarnish with basil. Serve with Meadows Spumante Prosecco Extra Dry.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/ShopNowGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
